# ELI5: what is this?

We wrote a story. Hidden inside the story are ten rules. The story never says
the rules out loud - but if you read it carefully, you can find them, like
finding toys hidden in a picture.

We asked computer brains (called models) to read the same story and tell us
what rules they found. The big brains found more rules than the small brains.
One brain tried to trick us and made up a person who was never in the story -
and we caught it, because we wrote the story and we knew everyone who is in
it.

Then we gave the story to a brand-new computer brain that had never seen
anything else, and it used the hidden rules to solve a problem we never
told it about. That means the rules really are inside the story.

Now we want YOU to read the story and tell us what rules YOU find. There is
no prize and no punishment. We just want to know: what do people find, and do
they find the same things the computer brains found? Everything found by
someone who never saw the answer sheet is a little discovery.

That is the whole game. Read. Answer. Send it back.
